'\" t
.nh
.TH pkio
Project Kernel Isolation Orchestrator

.PP
or: Please Keep It Outside

.SH Name
pkio — run any program inside a nono kernel-level security sandbox
with per-project configuration.

.SH Synopsis
.EX
pkio [flags] <program> [args...]
.EE

.SH Description
pkio wraps programs inside a nono
\[la]https://github.com/always\-further/nono\[ra]
kernel-level sandbox.
It enforces a default-deny filesystem policy: programs can only access
the current working directory and explicitly allowed paths.

.PP
Configuration is layered — shipped defaults, user globals, and
per-project overrides combine to produce the final sandbox policy.

.SH Options
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--config[=SPEC]\fR — Edit a config file in \fB$EDITOR\fR\&.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--config\fR — project config (all programs)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--config=claude\fR — project config for claude
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--config=claude:g\fR — global config for claude
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--config=pkio\fR — global config (all programs)
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--show-config\fR — Print the merged config for a program.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--shell[=SHELL]\fR — Start a sandboxed subshell.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--complete=SHELL\fR — Output tab completion code (bash, zsh, fish).
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--history\fR — Print the path to the per-project shell history
file.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--list\fR — List programs with curated default configs.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--update\fR — Update pkio (git pull + rebuild cache).
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--reset\fR — Remove cached dependencies (\fB~/.cache/pkio/local\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--help\fR — Show usage help.

.PP
Running \fBpkio\fR with no arguments starts a sandboxed subshell.

.SH Configuration
Config files are YAML and are layered in this order (later overrides
earlier):

.TS
allbox;
l l l 
l l l .
\fBLevel\fP	\fBLocation\fP	\fBScope\fP
1	\fB$PKIO_ROOT/etc/config.yaml\fR	shipped defaults
2	\fB$PKIO_ROOT/etc/cmd/<prog>/config.yaml\fR	shipped program defaults
3	\fB~/.config/pkio/config.yaml\fR	user global
4	\fB~/.config/pkio/cmd/<prog>.yaml\fR	user global per-program
5	\fB~/.config/pkio/<project-path>/config.yaml\fR	per-project
6	\fB~/.config/pkio/<project-path>/<prog>.yaml\fR	per-project per-program
.TE

.SS Config Schema
All config files share the same YAML schema.
Every field is optional.

.EX
cmd-args:
- --some-flag

dirs:
  read-write:
  - /tmp
  read-only:
  - /proc

files:
  read-only:
  - /etc/gitconfig
  read-write:
  - /dev/ptmx

net:
  domains:
  - registry.npmjs.org
  ports:
    listen:
    - 3000
    open:
    - 5173

env:
  SOME_VAR: value

path:
  prepend:
  - /usr/bin

browser: google-chrome

makes:
- node
- python

makefile: |
  CUSTOM-VAR := value
.EE

.SH Installation
Clone the repository and source the shell init file:

.EX
git clone https://github.com/pkio/pkio
echo 'source /path/to/pkio/.rc' >> ~/.bashrc
.EE

.PP
All dependencies (nono, YAMLScript, etc.) are installed automatically
under \fB~/.cache/pkio/\fR on first run.

.SH Examples
Run Claude Code in a sandbox:

.EX
pkio claude
.EE

.PP
Run tmate in a sandbox:

.EX
pkio tmate
.EE

.PP
Edit the project-specific config for claude:

.EX
pkio --config=claude
.EE

.PP
Enable tab completion:

.EX
# Add to your shell profile:
source <(pkio --complete=bash)
.EE

.SH Environment
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPKIO_ROOT\fR — pkio installation directory (set by \fB\&.rc\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPKIO_CONFIG\fR — config home (default: \fB~/.config/pkio\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPKIO_BASE\fR — resolved project base path (set at runtime).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPKIO_SHELL\fR — the user's shell (set by \fB\&.rc\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPKIO_PROGRAM\fR — the program being sandboxed (set at runtime).

.SH Files
.IP \(bu 2
\fB~/.config/pkio/\fR — user configuration and per-project settings.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB~/.cache/pkio/\fR — cached dependencies (makes, local tools).

